The chemistry strongly suggests zinc tungstate formation, but I’m treating that only as a candidate. I’m now extracting the observed peak positions/intensities and checking whether ZnWO₄ alone accounts for them or whether residual ZnO/WO₃ (or another crystalline component) is required.

The first refinement exposed two important issues: the peaks are much broader than a default laboratory profile, and simultaneous size/strain refinement was numerically ill-conditioned. I’ve switched to a broad common Caglioti profile (appropriate because no calibration file was supplied), staged the cell refinements, and seeded minor phases at low scale so they are tested rather than prematurely driven to zero.

Three crystalline phases are now supported independently: monoclinic WO₃ and ZnO both reduce the weighted residual and refine to plausible cells, while tetragonal/orthorhombic WO₃ and reduced tungsten oxides fit substantially worse. I’m now addressing systematic intensity mismatch (texture/profile effects) before accepting the quantitative fractions.

The three-phase model is now converged over every measured point. The current full refinement gives approximately 75.6 wt% ZnWO₄, 16.9 wt% monoclinic WO₃, and 7.6 wt% ZnO, with \(R_{wp}=5.48\%\) and no meaningful preferred orientation. I’m packaging the exact converged project and exports now, then I’ll validate that the CIFs reproduce the project contents and that all fractions/profile columns are internally consistent.

